[2026-10-27T11:36:14.223Z] [INFO]   "bodyPreview": "data: {\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"role\":\"assistant\"},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1793100973,\"id\":\"chatcmpl_a43ea61386e15278\",\"model\":\"formal-ai\",\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\"}\n\ndata: {\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{\"content\":\"Planificado, no ejecutado: https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/1446.\\n\\nEl trabajo solicitado sigue sin verificarse. El plan siguiente describe pasos previstos; escribir o leer un registro del plan no verifica la entrega. Plan:\\n\\n```lino\\ngeneral_change_plan\\n  id \\\"repository_work_item_plan_83c2eaceb8ee8f7a\\\"\\n  execution_mode \\\"repository_work_item\\\"\\n  terminal_state \\\"planned_not_executed\\\"\\n  goal \\\"Research & Implementation: Enhancing the Temperature and Randomization Mechanism via ProbabilityStore and Memory Dreaming\\\\n\\\\n### 1. Context & Theoretical Background\\\\nFollowing recent advancements in complexity theory (specifically the RL = L derandomization proof introduced in OpenAI's October 6, 2026 release), it is mathematically established that randomness does not grant additional computational power to bounded-memory algorithms. However, in engineering practice, incorporating controlled randomness (such as temperature) can significantly accelerate solution discovery, prevent local minima entrapment, and balance the trade-offs between strict deterministic exploration and heuristic acceleration.\\\\n\\\\nAs a symbolic, deterministic framework built on GOFAI traditions, Formal AI must reflect these principles realistically within its architecture, rather than mimicking LLM hyperparameter concepts on a surface level.\\\\n\\\\n### 2. Current Implementation Analysis & Facts\\\\nBased on the current codebase audit:\\\\n* **Deterministic Core:** The codebase relies on `rust/src/solver.rs::UniversalSolver`, which executes a strict 11-step loop (from impulse formalization to solution composition) for every prompt.\\\\n* **Non-Neural Architecture:** Knowledge is represented as an inspectable semantic network of human-readable links instead of hidden weights.\\\\n* **Existing Infrastructure:** The system already defines a `ProbabilityStore` capable of handling append-only Bayesian evidence and Markov transitions.\\\\n* **The Policy Gap:** While `ProbabilityStore` ranks symbolic candidate IDs before the temperature/clarify-vs-guess policy runs, the temperature parameter currently has a minimal impact on the runtime complexity and search behavior of the deterministic solvers (`solver.rs` and `solver_unknown_reasoning.rs`). At `temperature = 0`, the system should guarantee high-quality deterministic results (even if it takes longer), while `temperature > 0` should enable accelerated heuristic shortcuts based on probabilistic evidence.\\\\n\\\\n### 3. The Role of Memory Dreaming in Probabilistic Alignment\\\\nTo make this system truly dynamic and adaptive, the background **`memory dream`** mechanism (tracked under issue #540) must act as the primary engine for updating `ProbabilityStore`. \\\\n\\\\nWhile the core server is idle, the dreaming worker should analyze the interaction history with the user and the environment to **increase the baseline probability of obtaining the most relevant answers**. Instead of real-time weight calculations during a hot chat turn, `memory dream` will:\\\\n* Aggregate and compress the append-only event log into long-term statistical trends.\\\\n* Update Bayesian evidence inside the link-network, prioritizing paths, contexts, and rules that have historically led to verified, high-quality outcomes.\\\\n* Mine recurring multi-turn task structures, dynamically updating Markov transition probabilities so that future heuristic searches (`temperature > 0`) lean toward proven contextual pathways.\\\\n\\\\n### 4. Proposed Research Goals\\\\nWe need to conduct a deep dive into our solver mechanics to make the randomization/temperature behavior realistic and functional:\\\\n1. **Define `temperature = 0` Execution Path:** Ensure that at zero temperature, the `UniversalSolver` falls back to complete, exhaustive symbolic path traversal, ensuring maximum precision and deterministic accuracy, accepting the higher time/step cost if necessary.\\\\n2. **Implement Probabilistic Acceleration (`temperature > 0`):** Use the `ProbabilityStore` Markov transition weights to greedily prune or prioritize search paths within the link network, mimicking how higher temperature values allow algorithms to jump out of local minima or bypass exhaustive checking.\\\\n3. **Bridge Dreaming and ProbabilityStore:** Formally map the output of background `memory dream` analysis onto the active weights of the `ProbabilityStore`.\\\\n4. **Verify Contract Stability:** Ensure that enabling/disabling randomness or modifying temperature does not degrade the core symbolic verification pipelines pinned by our regression suites (e.g., HumanEval/MBPP controls, egg rewrite laws).\\\\n\\\\n### 5. Regression Control (`docs_benchmarks.rs`)\\\\nTo prevent future regressions and enforce the strict operational semantics of temperature settings, we must implement a dedicated unit/integration test within `rust/tests/unit/docs_benchmarks.rs`. This test will:\\\\n* Assert that a set of highly connected link subgraphs evaluated at `temperature = 0` successfully traverses all possible branches, returning exact results while validating the step/time cost.\\\\n* Assert that the same subgraph evaluated at `temperature > 0` with populated `ProbabilityStore` weights achieves a lower total step count (heuristic acceleration) without violating baseline correctness.\\\\n* Ensure any deviation from these committed architectural ledger entries causes a test failure (`rust/tests/unit/docs_benchmarks.rs` enforcement).\\\\n\\\\n### 6. Proposed Action Plan\\\\n* Audit `rust/src/solver.rs`, `rust/src/solver_unknown_reasoning.rs`, and the background dreaming worker to map out exact integration points for `ProbabilityStore`.\\\\n* Implement the new step-count validation test within `rust/tests/unit/docs_benchmarks.rs`.\\\\n* Document the findings and formalize the updated policy under `VISION.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md`.\\\"\\n  target \\\"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/1446\\\"\\n  step 1\\n    capability \\\"Fetch\\\"\\n    action \\\"read the referenced work item at https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/1446 before planning any change\\\"\\n    expected_evidence \\\"the work-item text naming the artifact the change must produce\\\"\\n  step 2\\n    capability \\\"Write\\\"\\n    action \\\"append the bounded repository work-item plan to .formal-ai/general-change-plan.lino\\\"\\n    expected_evidence \\\"the exact repository work-item goal and execution boundary\\\"\\n```\"},\"finish_reason\":null,\"index\":0}],\"created\":1793100973,\"id\":\"chatcmpl_a43ea61386e15278\",\"model\":\"formal-ai\",\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\"}\n\ndata: {\"choices\":[{\"delta\":{},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\",\"index\":0}],\"created\":1793100973,\"id\":\"chatcmpl_a43ea61386e15278\",\"model\":\"formal-ai\",\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\"}\n\ndata: {\"choices\":[],\"created\":1793100973,\"id\":\"chatcmpl_a43ea61386e15278\",\"model\":\"formal-ai\",\"object\":\"chat.completion.chunk\",\"usage\":{\"completion_tokens\":6296,\"prompt_tokens\":30537,\"total_tokens\":36833}}\n\ndata: [DONE]\n\n",
